{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And their children, who have not known, etc.</b> If this speaks of the young children who have reached the age of training, then it is well said: 'they shall hear, and learn to fear HaShem,' for they do not yet know anything of the matter of the fear of HaShem. But concerning the adults He said: 'that they may hear, and that they may learn, and fear HaShem' — for they need nothing but to hear and to learn the commandments, but as for the fear, they themselves will fear HaShem, for they have already grown accustomed to the fear of HaShem all the day. But if this verse speaks of the coming generations, it appears that one may explain it along the lines of what is said in parashat Eikev (Deuteronomy 10:12): 'And now, Israel, what does HaShem ask of you, but to fear' etc. — for it is written immediately after it: 'For it is not your children, who have not known and who have not seen the discipline of Elohim' etc., until 'but your eyes have seen all the great work of HaShem' — for he wanted to resolve by this what is written above: 'And now, Israel, what does HaShem your Elohim ask of you, but to fear' — is fear then a small matter? To this he said: had I been speaking with your children, who have not seen the discipline of HaShem and who are not rooted in the fear of HaShem, I would surely have been asking of them a very great thing; but I am speaking with you, whose eyes have seen all the work of HaShem which Elohim did, so that they would stand in awe before Him, as it is written (Exodus 20:17): 'and in order that His fear be upon your faces' etc., and with you, surely the thing I ask is small, for although fear is a thing of very great value, nevertheless with you it is easy to fulfill, for you are already rooted in fear. This is what he said: 'And now, Israel' — with the word 'and now' he sealed all his words, to say that now, in this generation, it is a small matter, and what does HaShem ask of you now but to fear. And this is what is said here concerning that generation: 'that they may hear, and that they may learn, and fear HaShem' — for regarding the fear they do not need such exhortation, and of themselves they will fear HaShem. 'And their children, who have not known' — exactly like the statement 'For it is not your children, who have not known' etc. — and by this he meant: your children, who have not known the discipline of HaShem and have not seen His greatness, they need exhortation and learning concerning the fear. And this is what he said: 'they shall hear, and learn to fear HaShem' — for with them the fear is a very great thing."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:15:23.151764961Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}